<article class="env-lemma" id="08RU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08RU">Lemma <span data-tag="08RU">17.28.12</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X' \ar[d]_{h'} \ar[r]_ f &  X \ar[d]^ h \\  S' \ar[r]^ g &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of ringed spaces. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The canonical map $\mathcal{O}_ X \to f_*\mathcal{O}_{X'}$ composed with $f_*\text{d}_{X'/S'} : f_*\mathcal{O}_{X'} \to f_*\Omega _{X'/S'}$ is a $S$-derivation and we obtain a canonical map of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $\Omega _{X/S} \to f_*\Omega _{X'/S'}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ X \ar[r] &  \mathcal{O}_{X'} \\  f^{-1}h^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ S \ar[u] \ar[r] &  (h')^{-1}\mathcal{O}_{S'} \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
<p>
 induces by Lemmas <a href="/tag/08RR" data-tag="08RR">17.28.6</a> and <a href="/tag/08RS" data-tag="08RS">17.28.8</a> a canonical map $f^{-1}\Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{X'/S'}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> These two maps correspond (via adjointness of $f_*$ and $f^*$ and via $f^*\Omega _{X/S} = f^{-1}\Omega _{X/S} \otimes _{f^{-1}\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{O}_{X'}$ and Sheaves, Lemma <a href="/tag/008A" data-tag="008A">6.20.2</a>) to the same $\mathcal{O}_{X'}$-module homomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c_ f : f^*\Omega _{X/S} \longrightarrow \Omega _{X'/S'}  \]
</div>
  <p> which is uniquely characterized by the property that $f^*\text{d}_{X/S}(a)$ maps to $\text{d}_{X'/S'}(f^*a)$ for any local section $a$ of $\mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>